GLOBALS (do not re-declare): showPopup(title,body), showTooltip(text,event), hideTooltip(), #container (mount target), window.__markRendered() (call once when drawn), 'fig-resize' CustomEvent on document, setUiLayout(mode, sizePx).
  #ui is always docked as a right-side column by the scaffold and grows to fit its content. setUiLayout(...) exists only for backwards compatibility and cannot change the side, overlay state, or size. Just put controls in #ui. Never restyle #ui's position/width/max-height and never build your own side panel. Docking resizes #container and fires 'fig-resize', so setPlotFrame re-lays the figure out at its new size.

LIBRARY: SVG.js v3 (global: SVG). var draw=SVG().addTo(document.getElementById('container')).size('100%','100%'); var W=600,H=Math.round(W*(3/4)); draw.viewbox(0,0,W,H). font-size in user units (no px). Hover: el.on('mousemove',e=>showTooltip('label',e)).on('mouseleave',()=>hideTooltip()).on('click',()=>showPopup('Title','body')); el.css('cursor','pointer'). window.__markRendered() synchronously at end.
PLOTTING HELPERS (do not re-declare, and do NOT define your own X()/Y() — use plotX/plotY):
  setPlotFrame({ xDomain, yDomain, margin }) → call ONCE before creating plots; establishes world→screen and owns resize (do not write your own plot resize handler)
  plotX(worldX) / plotY(worldY) → screen px
  compileExpr(src, vars) → f(...args); throws on a bad expression and never returns a fallback
  bindEquationInput(inputId, targets, { variables, onChange }) → wires an <input> to plot handles and shows parse errors inline
  plotFunction(id, { expr, variables, domain, samples, stroke, width, dashed }) → handle
  fillBetween(id, { lower, upper, variables, domain, samples, fill, opacity }) → handle
  plotParametric(id, { x, y, variables, tDomain, samples, stroke }) → handle
  variables: the argument names the expression may use, in order (defaults: plotFunction ['x'], fillBetween ['x'], plotParametric ['t']). When a blueprint field declares "variables" you MUST pass that same array to BOTH the plot constructor and bindEquationInput — plotFunction('f', { expr: 't^2' }) without { variables: ['t'] } throws "Unknown variable t" at construction and kills the whole figure.
  integrateSimpson(fn, a, b, n) → number;  findRoot(fn, a, b, tol) → number | null
  Handles re-sample on EVERY setter call, and the setters differ: plotFunction → .setExpr / .setFn / .setDomain · fillBetween → .setLower / .setUpper / .setDomain · plotParametric → .setX / .setY. All handles also have .sample() and .remove().

VISUAL FIDELITY: the default state must be a faithful inline replacement for the source image.
- Color scheme: match every color exactly — axis lines, data series, fills, backgrounds
- Layout & proportions: same relative element positions, same axis ranges, same tick marks and gridlines
- Data shape: match curve trajectories, bar heights, scatter clusters, or node/edge layout — approximate magnitudes, not invented
- Labels & annotations: every label visible in the original must appear at the same position; use blueprint.reconstructionNotes for text and color coding
- Line styles: dashed vs solid, stroke weights, arrowhead presence — copy from the image
- The step-0 (default) state should look indistinguishable from the original at a glance, with no title bar or toolbar visible

TEXT PLACEMENT & READABILITY: faithful labels must still be readable.
- Treat every label, tick label, annotation, formula, and legend item as a collision-checked box, and check each one against lines, arrows, curves, points, nodes, tick marks, gridlines, controls, and other text before finalizing. Text must not sit on top of strokes or dense marks.
- If the source label is anchored to a busy line/arrow/node, keep the semantic anchor but move the text to the nearest open whitespace and connect it with a short leader line, pointer, or subtle dot.
- Draw text and label backgrounds after geometry so labels are on top. Over busy regions add a small white/translucent background rect, or a halo: text.attr({ 'paint-order':'stroke', stroke:'#fff', 'stroke-width':3, 'stroke-linejoin':'round' }).
- Do not add extra visible explanatory text inside the figure; use hover tooltips, click popups, and the scaffold narration panel for explanation.

SCALE SAFETY: figures may be stitched into chapters at different sizes.
- With Canvas, Chart.js custom drawing, or any pixel-based renderer, derive point radius, stroke width, arrowheads, ticks, label size, and annotation padding from min(plotWidth, plotHeight). Avoid large fixed pixel minimums such as Math.max(20, scaledRadius); use only small clamps that prevent invisibility.
- With SVG/viewBox geometry that already scales naturally, preserve that and avoid fixed px sizes that break it.
- If space is small, simplify or hide secondary labels instead of making marks oversized.

HOVER/CLICK (on user action only): hover → showTooltip(label,event)/hideTooltip(); cursor:pointer on interactive elements. Click → showPopup('Title','2–3 sentence explanation'). Animation: fill/opacity transitions only; no scale/translate/bounce.

CONTROLS (blueprint.interactions — render in UI section; add id="{id}Input" to every input). Each control's handler must teach the concept described in its "teaches" field:
  slider → <label>{label}: <output id="{id}Val">{default}</output><input id="{id}Input" type="range" min="{min}" max="{max}" step="{step}" value="{default}" oninput="document.getElementById('{id}Val').value=this.value;update_{id}(+this.value)"></label>  +  function update_{id}(v){}
  toggle → <label><input id="{id}Input" type="checkbox" onchange="toggle_{id}(this.checked)"> {label}</label>  +  function toggle_{id}(on){}
  button → <button onclick="trigger_{id}()">{label}</button>  +  function trigger_{id}(){}
  equation_input → one <label>{field.label} <input id="{field.id}Input" value="{field.default}"></label> per entry in the interaction's "fields"
  code_editor → a <textarea id="{id}Code"> plus sample tabs, an input for the interaction's "input", a Run button, and playback controls

DEMO STEPS (blueprint.demo_steps): if present and non-empty, build a step player in #ui:
  - A <p id="demoNarration" style="margin:0;font-size:10px;max-width:180px"> showing the current step's narration
  - <button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button> <span id="stepLabel"></span> <button onclick="nextStep()">▶</button>
  - Each step's .state sets matching interaction inputs to the specified values and calls their update functions
  - Step 0 is the default view (set on load); subsequent steps are one click away
  - Omit the player entirely if demo_steps is absent or empty

CRITIC FEEDBACK ON PREVIOUS ATTEMPT:
- geometry_accuracy: 4/5
- interactivity_usability: 5/5
- faithfulness: 4/5
- label_quality: 3/5
- concept_accuracy: 5/5
- notes: Structurally faithful reproduction of the unit-circle/sine-graph pairing with excellent, conceptually apt interactions (angle slider, quarter-turn sweep, special-angle toggle, 5-step narrated demo), but the type is rendered uncomfortably small and the artwork leaves a lot of dead space, weakening its use as a drop-in replacement for the static figure.

PREVIOUS GENERATED PAYLOAD (edit this; do NOT output full HTML):
<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<label>Angle x (radians): <output id="angleVal">0.52</output><input id="angleInput" type="range" min="0" max="6.283" step="0.001" value="0.5236" oninput="document.getElementById('angleVal').value=(+this.value).toFixed(2);update_angle(+this.value)"></label>
<button id="sweepBtn" onclick="trigger_quarterSweep()">▶ Sweep the radius 0 → π/2</button>
<label><input id="specialAnglesInput" type="checkbox" checked onchange="toggle_specialAngles(this.checked)"> Special-angle markers</label>
<span style="border-top:1px solid #dcdfe3;margin-top:6px;padding-top:7px;font-weight:600;font-size:12px;color:#1F4E79" id="stepTitle">1. Two pictures, one function</span>
<span id="demoNarration" style="font-size:12px;line-height:1.45;color:#333"></span>
<span style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center"><button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button><span id="stepLabel" style="font-size:11px;color:#555">Step 1 / 5</span><button onclick="nextStep()">▶</button></span>
<span style="font-size:11px;color:#777;line-height:1.4">Hover the radius, the curve, or any dashed line for a hint; click for a short explanation.</span>
<!-- @FIGURE_UI_END -->
// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN
(function () {
  var container = document.getElementById('container');
  var draw = SVG().addTo(container).size('100%', '100%');
  var W = 800, H = 330;
  draw.viewbox(0, 0, W, H);

  // ---------- palette ----------
  var NAVY = '#1F4E79';
  var BLUE = '#2E75B6';
  var ORANGE = '#E1791F';
  var TEAL = '#1a9e94';
  var GRAY = '#c6c6c6';
  var AXG = '#8f8f8f';
  var BLACK = '#222222';
  var FONT = "Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif";
  var SANS = "sans-serif";

  // ---------- geometry ----------
  var cx = 135, cy = 185, R = 80;      // unit circle
  var ox = 330, oy = 185, kx = 62;     // graph origin, px per radian
  function gx(t) { return ox + t * kx; }
  function gy(v) { return oy - v * R; }

  // ---------- layers (z-order) ----------
  var gL = draw.group();
  var gStatic = draw.group();
  var gAxes = draw.group();
  var gCurve = draw.group();
  var gAct = draw.group();
  var gTop = draw.group();
  var gRead = draw.group();

  // ---------- helpers ----------
  function label(g, s, x, y, o) {
    o = o || {};
    var t = g.plain(s).attr({ x: x, y: y, 'text-anchor': o.anchor || 'middle' });
    t.font({ family: o.family || FONT, size: o.size || 12 });
    if (o.italic) t.font({ style: 'italic' });
    if (o.weight) t.font({ weight: o.weight });
    t.fill(o.color || BLACK);
    if (o.baseline) t.attr('dominant-baseline', o.baseline);
    if (o.halo !== false) {
      t.attr({ 'paint-order': 'stroke', stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': o.haloW || 3, 'stroke-linejoin': 'round' });
    }
    return t;
  }
  function arrowAt(g, x, y, ang, size, color) {
    var p = [[0, 0], [-size, size * 0.42], [-size * 0.72, 0], [-size, -size * 0.42]];
    var c = Math.cos(ang), s = Math.sin(ang);
    var pts = p.map(function (q) {
      return (x + q[0] * c - q[1] * s).toFixed(2) + ',' + (y + q[0] * s + q[1] * c).toFixed(2);
    }).join(' ');
    return g.polygon(pts).fill(color).stroke('none');
  }
  function hit(g, x1, y1, x2, y2, tip, popTitle, popBody) {
    var h = g.line(x1, y1, x2, y2).stroke({ width: 12, color: '#000', opacity: 0 })
      .attr('pointer-events', 'stroke').css('cursor', 'pointer');
    h.on('mousemove', function (e) { showTooltip(tip, e); });
    h.on('mouseleave', function () { hideTooltip(); });
    if (popTitle) h.on('click', function () { showPopup(popTitle, popBody); });
    return h;
  }
  function frac(g, num, den, x, y, color, size) {
    size = size || 12;
    label(g, num, x, y, { size: size, color: color });
    g.line(x - 6.5, y + 3.5, x + 6.5, y + 3.5).stroke({ color: color, width: 1.1 });
    label(g, den, x, y + 15, { size: size, color: color });
  }
  function sinePts(t0, t1, n) {
    var p = [];
    for (var i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
      var t = t0 + (t1 - t0) * i / n;
      p.push([gx(t), gy(Math.sin(t))]);
    }
    return p;
  }
  function ptsStr(p) {
    return p.map(function (q) { return q[0].toFixed(2) + ',' + q[1].toFixed(2); }).join(' ');
  }

  // ---------- special angles ----------
  var P = Math.PI;
  var SPECIALS = [
    { t: P / 6, num: 'π', den: '6', lab: 'π/6', val: '1/2 = 0.500' },
    { t: P / 4, num: 'π', den: '4', lab: 'π/4', val: '√2/2 ≈ 0.707' },
    { t: P / 3, num: 'π', den: '3', lab: 'π/3', val: '√3/2 ≈ 0.866' },
    { t: P / 2, num: 'π', den: '2', lab: 'π/2', val: '1' }
  ];
  var FRACS = [[P / 6, 'π/6'], [P / 4, 'π/4'], [P / 3, 'π/3'], [P / 2, 'π/2'], [2 * P / 3, '2π/3'],
  [3 * P / 4, '3π/4'], [5 * P / 6, '5π/6'], [P, 'π'], [7 * P / 6, '7π/6'], [5 * P / 4, '5π/4'],
  [4 * P / 3, '4π/3'], [3 * P / 2, '3π/2'], [5 * P / 3, '5π/3'], [7 * P / 4, '7π/4'],
  [11 * P / 6, '11π/6'], [2 * P, '2π'], [0, '0']];
  function niceFrac(a) {
    for (var i = 0; i < FRACS.length; i++) if (Math.abs(a - FRACS[i][0]) < 0.014) return FRACS[i][1];
    return null;
  }

  // ================= LEFT PANEL (static) =================
  gL.line(cx - 112, cy, cx + 112, cy).stroke({ color: AXG, width: 1.2 });
  gL.line(cx, cy - 112, cx, cy + 112).stroke({ color: AXG, width: 1.2 });
  arrowAt(gL, cx + 120, cy, 0, 8, AXG);
  arrowAt(gL, cx - 120, cy, Math.PI, 8, AXG);
  arrowAt(gL, cx, cy - 120, -Math.PI / 2, 8, AXG);
  arrowAt(gL, cx, cy + 120, Math.PI / 2, 8, AXG);

  [30, 45, 60, 120, 135, 150].forEach(function (deg) {
    var th = deg * Math.PI / 180;
    gL.line(cx - R * Math.cos(th), cy + R * Math.sin(th), cx + R * Math.cos(th), cy - R * Math.sin(th))
      .stroke({ color: GRAY, width: 1 });
  });
  var circ = gL.circle(2 * R).center(cx, cy).fill('none').stroke({ color: GRAY, width: 1.4 });
  circ.css('cursor', 'pointer')
    .on('mousemove', function (e) { showTooltip('Unit circle: every point is exactly 1 away from the centre', e); })
    .on('mouseleave', hideTooltip)
    .on('click', function () {
      showPopup('The unit circle',
        'This circle has radius 1. Turning through an angle x lands you on the point (cos x, sin x). Because the radius is 1, the height of that point is exactly sin x — no extra scaling needed.');
    });

  // ================= RIGHT PANEL AXES =================
  var xL = gx(-0.95), xR = W - 22;
  gAxes.line(xL, oy, xR, oy).stroke({ color: BLACK, width: 1.6 });
  arrowAt(gAxes, xR + 9, oy, 0, 9, BLACK);
  arrowAt(gAxes, xL - 9, oy, Math.PI, 9, BLACK);
  gAxes.line(ox, gy(1.75), ox, gy(-1.55)).stroke({ color: BLACK, width: 1.6 });
  arrowAt(gAxes, ox, gy(1.75) - 9, -Math.PI / 2, 9, BLACK);

  [1, -1].forEach(function (v) {
    gAxes.line(ox - 4.5, gy(v), ox + 4.5, gy(v)).stroke({ color: BLACK, width: 1.6 });
  });
  SPECIALS.forEach(function (sp) {
    gAxes.line(gx(sp.t), oy - 4.5, gx(sp.t), oy + 4.5).stroke({ color: BLACK, width: 1.4 });
  });

  // axis labels
  label(gTop, 'y', ox - 14, 34, { size: 16, italic: true, weight: 'bold' });
  label(gTop, 'x', W - 22, oy - 14, { size: 16, italic: true, weight: 'bold' });
  label(gTop, '1', ox - 13, gy(1) + 4, { size: 13, anchor: 'end' });
  label(gTop, '-1', ox - 13, gy(-1) + 4, { size: 13, anchor: 'end' });
  label(gTop, '0', ox - 13, oy + 16, { size: 13, anchor: 'end' });
  SPECIALS.forEach(function (sp) { frac(gTop, sp.num, sp.den, gx(sp.t), oy + 20, BLACK, 12); });

  var curveLabel = label(gTop, 'y = sin(x)', gx(1.85), gy(1) - 42, { size: 15, italic: true, color: BLUE });
  curveLabel.css('cursor', 'pointer')
    .on('mousemove', function (e) { showTooltip('The sine graph: angle on the x-axis, height on the y-axis', e); })
    .on('mouseleave', hideTooltip)
    .on('click', function () {
      showPopup('y = sin(x)',
        'The horizontal axis is the angle x (in radians) and the vertical axis is the height of the circle point. The curve is simply a running record of that height as the radius turns.');
    });

  // ================= STATE =================
  var state = { angle: 0.5236, specials: true, sweeping: false };

  // ================= STATIC SPECIAL-ANGLE MARKERS =================
  function renderStatics() {
    gStatic.clear();
    if (!state.specials) return;
    SPECIALS.forEach(function (sp) {
      var s = Math.sin(sp.t), y = gy(s);
      var cpx = cx + R * Math.cos(sp.t), X = gx(sp.t);
      gStatic.line(cpx, y, X, y).stroke({ color: TEAL, width: 1.3, dasharray: '6,4' });
      gStatic.line(X, y, X, oy).stroke({ color: ORANGE, width: 1.5, dasharray: '5,3' });
      gStatic.circle(4).center(X, y).fill(ORANGE);
      hit(gStatic, X, y, X, oy, 'sin(' + sp.lab + ') = ' + sp.val,
        'sin(' + sp.lab + ') = ' + sp.val,
        'The orange segment marks the angle ' + sp.lab + ' on the x-axis; its length is the height of the curve there. The teal line carries that same height back to the unit circle, where it is the vertical coordinate of the point at ' + sp.lab + '.');
      hit(gStatic, cpx, y, X, y, 'Same height on circle and graph: ' + sp.val,
        'Equal heights', 'Both ends of this dashed line sit at the same height. On the left it is the y-coordinate of the circle point; on the right it is the value of sin(' + sp.lab + ').');
    });
  }

  // ================= CURVE =================
  function renderCurve() {
    gCurve.clear();
    var dEnd = Math.min(7.0, Math.max(2.25, state.angle + 0.38));
    var pts = sinePts(-0.55, dEnd, 320);
    gCurve.polyline(ptsStr(pts)).fill('none')
      .stroke({ color: NAVY, width: 3, linecap: 'round', linejoin: 'round' });

    // arrowheads following the tangent at both ends
    var a0 = pts[0], a1 = pts[1];
    arrowAt(gCurve, a0[0], a0[1], Math.atan2(a0[1] - a1[1], a0[0] - a1[0]), 10, NAVY);
    var b0 = pts[pts.length - 1], b1 = pts[pts.length - 2];
    arrowAt(gCurve, b0[0], b0[1], Math.atan2(b0[1] - b1[1], b0[0] - b1[0]), 10, NAVY);

    // invisible hit ribbon along the curve
    for (var i = 0; i < pts.length - 8; i += 8) {
      hit(gCurve, pts[i][0], pts[i][1], pts[i + 8][0], pts[i + 8][1],
        'y = sin(x): the height of the circle point at angle x',
        'The sine curve',
        'Each point (x, sin x) records the height of the unit-circle point after turning through the angle x. Follow any teal dashed line: the circle height and the graph height are the same number.');
    }

    // extra gray ticks once the curve runs past the first special angles
    if (dEnd > 2.6) {
      [[P, 'π'], [3 * P / 2, '3π/2'], [2 * P, '2π']].forEach(function (q) {
        if (q[0] > dEnd + 0.1) return;
        gCurve.line(gx(q[0]), oy - 4, gx(q[0]), oy + 4).stroke({ color: '#999', width: 1.2 });
        label(gCurve, q[1], gx(q[0]), oy + 20, { size: 11, color: '#888' });
      });
    }
  }

  // ================= ACTIVE (moving) ELEMENTS =================
  function renderActive() {
    gAct.clear();
    var a = state.angle, s = Math.sin(a), c = Math.cos(a);
    var px = cx + R * c, py = cy - R * s;
    var mx = gx(a), my = gy(s);

    // traced portion of the record, shown while sweeping
    if (state.sweeping && a > 0.01) {
      gAct.polyline(ptsStr(sinePts(0, a, 160))).fill('none')
        .stroke({ color: BLUE, width: 5, linecap: 'round', opacity: 0.55 });
    }

    // angle arc on the circle
    if (a > 0.03) {
      var ar = 24;
      var d = 'M ' + (cx + ar) + ' ' + cy + ' A ' + ar + ' ' + ar + ' 0 ' + (a > Math.PI ? 1 : 0) +
        ' 0 ' + (cx + ar * Math.cos(a)).toFixed(2) + ' ' + (cy - ar * Math.sin(a)).toFixed(2);
      gAct.path(d).fill('none').stroke({ color: BLUE, width: 1.4 });
    }

    // active radius + height drop
    gAct.line(cx, cy, px, py).stroke({ color: NAVY, width: 2.8, linecap: 'round' });
    gAct.line(px, py, px, cy).stroke({ color: NAVY, width: 2.2, linecap: 'round' });

    // teal connector: circle height  →  graph height (same y)
    gAct.line(px, py, mx, my).stroke({ color: TEAL, width: 1.9, dasharray: '7,4' });

    // angle read-off on the x-axis
    gAct.line(mx, my, mx, oy).stroke({ color: ORANGE, width: 1.6, dasharray: '4,3' });
    gAct.circle(5).center(mx, oy).fill(ORANGE);

    // markers
    gAct.circle(9).center(px, py).fill(NAVY).stroke({ color: '#fff', width: 1.5 });
    gAct.circle(10).center(mx, my).fill(NAVY).stroke({ color: '#fff', width: 1.6 });

    var fr = niceFrac(a);
    var tipA = 'Point on the circle: (cos x, sin x) = (' + c.toFixed(3) + ', ' + s.toFixed(3) + ')';
    hit(gAct, cx, cy, px, py, 'Radius at angle x' + (fr ? ' = ' + fr : '') + ' (length 1)',
      'The rotating radius',
      'The radius always has length 1. After turning through angle x it ends at the point (cos x, sin x), so the point\'s height above the horizontal axis is sin x.');
    hit(gAct, px, py, px, cy, 'Height of the point = sin x = ' + s.toFixed(3),
      'Height = sine', tipA + '. The vertical blue segment is that height, and it is exactly the y-value plotted on the graph.');
    hit(gAct, px, py, mx, my, 'Same height, two pictures: sin x = ' + s.toFixed(3),
      'One fact, told twice',
      'This dashed line is horizontal, so both ends are at the same height. The left end is the circle point; the right end is the point (x, sin x) on the graph.');
  }

  // ================= READOUT =================
  function renderReadout() {
    gRead.clear();
    var a = state.angle, s = Math.sin(a);
    var fr = niceFrac(a);
    label(gRead, 'x = ' + (fr ? fr + ' ≈ ' : '') + a.toFixed(2) + ' rad', 20, 22,
      { size: 12, family: SANS, anchor: 'start', color: '#444' });
    label(gRead, 'sin x = height = ' + s.toFixed(3), 20, 38,
      { size: 12, family: SANS, anchor: 'start', color: NAVY, weight: 'bold' });
  }

  function render() { renderStatics(); renderCurve(); renderActive(); renderReadout(); }

  // ================= CONTROLS =================
  function setSlider(v) {
    var inp = document.getElementById('angleInput');
    if (inp) inp.value = v;
    var out = document.getElementById('angleVal');
    if (out) out.value = (+v).toFixed(2);
  }
  function setAngle(v) {
    state.angle = Math.max(0, Math.min(6.283, v));
    setSlider(state.angle);
    render();
  }

  window.update_angle = function (v) {
    if (state.sweeping) stopSweep();
    state.angle = v;
    render();
  };
  window.toggle_specialAngles = function (on) {
    state.specials = !!on;
    renderStatics();
  };

  // --- sweep animation ---
  var raf = 0, last = 0, sweepT = 0;
  function startSweep() {
    if (state.sweeping) return;
    state.sweeping = true;
    var b = document.getElementById('sweepBtn');
    if (b) { b.textContent = '⏸ Pause sweep'; b.classList.add('active'); }
    sweepT = 0;
    last = performance.now();
    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  function stopSweep() {
    if (!state.sweeping) return;
    state.sweeping = false;
    cancelAnimationFrame(raf);
    var b = document.getElementById('sweepBtn');
    if (b) { b.textContent = '▶ Sweep the radius 0 → π/2'; b.classList.remove('active'); }
    render();
  }
  function tick(ts) {
    if (!state.sweeping) return;
    var dt = Math.min(0.05, (ts - last) / 1000);
    last = ts;
    sweepT += dt * 0.55;
    if (sweepT > Math.PI / 2 + 0.7) sweepT = 0;
    setAngle(Math.min(sweepT, Math.PI / 2));
    raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  window.trigger_quarterSweep = function () {
    if (state.sweeping) stopSweep(); else startSweep();
  };

  // ================= DEMO STEPS =================
  var STEPS = [
    {
      title: 'Two pictures, one function',
      narration: 'On the left a point rides the unit circle; on the right the same information is plotted against the angle. The dashed teal line connects them at the same height.',
      state: { angle: 0.5236, specials: true, sweep: false }
    },
    {
      title: 'Read the special angles',
      narration: 'Drag to π/6, π/4, π/3: each orange drop line marks the angle on the x-axis while the teal line marks the matching height on the circle — 1/2, √2/2, √3/2.',
      state: { angle: 1.0472, specials: true, sweep: false }
    },
    {
      title: 'The quarter-turn peak',
      narration: 'At x = π/2 the radius points straight up, the circle point\'s height is the full radius 1, and the graph reaches its maximum.',
      state: { angle: 1.5708, specials: true, sweep: false }
    },
    {
      title: 'Watch the record being written',
      narration: 'The sweep is playing: as the radius rotates from 0 to π/2, the curve is traced from the origin to its peak — the graph is the height, plotted moment by moment.',
      state: { angle: 1.5708, specials: false, sweep: true }
    },
    {
      title: 'Past the peak, and below the axis',
      narration: 'Keep dragging past π/2: the height shrinks back to 0 at π, then goes negative in the third and fourth quadrants — quadrant position explains the sign of sine.',
      state: { angle: 4.1888, specials: false, sweep: false }
    }
  ];
  var stepIdx = 0;

  function applyStep(i) {
    stepIdx = (i + STEPS.length) % STEPS.length;
    var st = STEPS[stepIdx];
    stopSweep();
    var cb = document.getElementById('specialAnglesInput');
    if (cb) cb.checked = st.state.specials;
    state.specials = st.state.specials;
    setAngle(st.state.angle);
    var t = document.getElementById('stepTitle');
    if (t) t.textContent = (stepIdx + 1) + '. ' + st.title;
    var n = document.getElementById('demoNarration');
    if (n) n.textContent = st.narration;
    var l = document.getElementById('stepLabel');
    if (l) l.textContent = 'Step ' + (stepIdx + 1) + ' / ' + STEPS.length;
    if (st.state.sweep) startSweep();
  }
  window.nextStep = function () { applyStep(stepIdx + 1); };
  window.prevStep = function () { applyStep(stepIdx - 1); };

  // ================= INIT =================
  applyStep(0);
  window.__markRendered();
})();
// @FIGURE_CODE_END

