userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The sine of an angle is the height (y-coordinate) of the corresponding point on the unit circle, so the graph of y = sin(x) is a running record of that height as the angle turns.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): sin(x) is not a new quantity to memorize — it is literally the vertical height of the unit-circle point at angle x, and the sine graph is that height plotted against the angle.
DEMO STEPS: 5 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
